add('All six cells have usable fractions 1.000 under the 0.10 alphabet-mass gate. Five intervals lie below the corresponding forward reliability reference; Qwen/Pavlick includes its reference. The fresh paired extraction records pinned revisions and prompt/token provenance, and its forward arm reproduces canonical ordering at ρ=0.9991–0.9999. It reran both orientations rather than using the unreferenced legacy reverse cache. The fresh evidence is five-of-six failure under the stated rule, not ρ≈0 in every cell. The reliability reference itself is treated as the saved point reference by this rule. Sources: ' + link('cached_results/letter11_provenance_v1/summary.csv') + ' and ' + link('cached_results/letter11_provenance_v1/README.md') + '.')

